snp4.6:7.1 starts: A monk, living withdrawn,
snp4.16:5.3 starts: at which he shouldn’t tremble
snp4.16:5.4 starts: —there in his noiseless abode—
snp4.16:8.1 starts: Undertaking what training
snp3.1:14.4 starts: and on arrival sat down.
snp3.1:15.1 starts: Sitting there, he exchanged courteous greetings,
thag2.37:1.3 starts: The night, for one who knows,
an4.159:4.2 starts: food is to be abandoned.
an4.159:4.4 starts: craving is to be abandoned.
an4.159:4.6 starts: conceit is to be abandoned.
